		{"id":"52fc8125884b207a","type":"text","text":"# Alex Paige\nAge: 15\n#### Basic Traits\n- **Age:** 15\n- **Birthday:** June 06\n\t- This is the summer solstice\n- **Gender/Identity:** Female | She/her\n","x":-340,"y":-380,"width":380,"height":400},
		{"id":"01cee97d580d28aa","type":"text","text":"## Character Interview (Book One)\n#### What is your name?\nAlex Paige. Okay, technically it’s ‘Alexandra’, but please don’t call me that.\n#### Do you have any nicknames? Who gave them to you?\nMy Dad calls me Al. It’s not much longer than Alex, but I guess it’s his way of showing some sort of endearment or whatever.\n\nI was called the *Soda Witch* because of an incident in middle school. I, uh, thought it was cool at first. But then people stopped being around me, and I started to hate it.\n#### How old are you now?\nFifteen years too many.\n#### When were you born?\nFifteen years ago? Duh. \n#### Where do you call your home?\nI guess...with my Dad. Though I haven’t really spent time in his apartment for quite some time. My ‘home’ tends to be wherever I find myself at the moment. The many different schools I’ve been sent to.\n\nMaybe the *cabin* could be considered a home. It feels like the only place to relax throughout the year.\n#### To what social class do you belong?\nYou mean like how rich we are? Not at all. Okay, well, I guess my Dad must make some sort of money cause he can afford to live in New York AND send me to a different private school every year after I get expelled.\n\nI don’t particularly *feel* well off, but we must have some sort of money.\n#### What is your eye color?\nGreen. Like, seaweed green.\n#### What is your hair color?\nA dull gray. My Dad likes to explain that it “shines like silver”, but I don’t see it. It’s the only thing to remind me of my mother, so It’s not the best.\n#### Do you have any distinguishing facial features?\nmmmmm, I have freckles? Its not that distinguishing, but I got them from my Dad. The gray hair overrode the red that I would have gotten from my Dad, but I was at least left with a face of light freckles.\n#### Do you have any birthmarks?\nNot that I know of. I have this dent in my head, but I think I was just dropped as a baby.\n#### Do you have any scars?\nNo. Even though so many weird things have happened to me over the course of my life. It continues to surprise me at how little damage I sustain. \n#### Do you have any tattoos or other markings?\nNo. I’m not really old enough to get any tattoos. Plus, Dad seems deathly afraid of me going anywhere near tattoo parlors. For some reason he avoids them like the plague. Just a protective parent, I guess.\n#### Do you have any allergies, diseases, or physical weaknesses?\nI’m allergic to vegetables. Okay, not really. I’m just picky. My Dad has told me that his side of the family has a history of diabetes, but I don’t have anything like that.\n#### Are you right or left handed?\nuhh-\\*holds up hands\\*-right.\n#### What does your voice sound like?\nTo me, I guess a little high. But not like a soft high like a flute. More like a trumpet. Brash and loud.\n#### How do you dress most of the time?\nHoodies and loose clothing. I’ve worn some school uniforms before and I hate it. They always feel tight and suffocating. I don’t mind skirts, but only if I can also wear some pants underneath.\n#### How do you dress up?\nI don’t ever remember dressing up. They’ve had formals and dances in school, but I never attended. Not like I would have been invited by anyone in the first place. \n\nI’ve always thought that It would be nice to wear a big frilly dress. At least once. It would probably be suffocating, but Idk.\n#### How do you dress down?\nPajamas, a big t-shirt, and a snuggie with the fur inside. I would always dress like that when we spent time in the cabin. It was warm in the loft with the fire going. It allowed me to relax and read books with Dad. Good memories.\n#### What do you wear when you go to sleep?\nI just explained it, I guess.\n#### Do you wear any jewelry?\nMy dad gave me a necklace once, but It broke almost immediately. Since then I haven’t really worn anything. It either tends to break from my misfortune or I lose it.\n#### What words or phrases do you use frequently?\nYike. Singular, not plural. I guess I tend to curse, but mostly to myself.\n#### Do you have any quirks, strange mannerisms, annoying habits, or defining characteristics?\nHow am I supposed to know that? Or even be objective about it? Um, I guess I fight back a lot. With words, I don’t know how to fight with fists. I’m sarcastic, probably.\n#### Do you have any bad habits?\nWould sarcasm also count as a bad habit? I tend to use it more when I don’t want to talk about something. It’s...easier.","x":-760,"y":40,"width":800,"height":940},
		{"id":"4b4788c9421fa5c1","type":"text","text":"## Abilities\nAlex’s abilities are mostly focused around her affinity for light magic since it’s powerful by itself. She mostly uses her crest to augment her abilities and support her manifestation.\n\n#### Manifestation\nHer manifestation allows for Alex to adjust the density and frequency of light in a certain range of her choosing. She can dictate an area as the center and the effects take place in a spherical radius around her.\n- **Red Shift**: This happens by decreasing the frequency of light in an area.\n\t- **Heat:** When she increases the density of these low frequency waves, the thermal head generated eventually turns the surrounding matter into plasma.\n\t- **Cold**: While decreasing the intensity of the waves in an area, she can reduce the temperature, creating near-vacuum like cold spots.\n\t- **Electronic Interference:** Through decreasing the frequency of waves in the area, it can mess with certain electronic sensors such as cameras and other technology dependent on UV light.\n\t- **Bending Light**: Through adjusting the density and decreasing the frequency of the light around her or an object, she can cause it to become invisible to the naked eye. It still emits head so it can be picked up by infrared sensing.\n- **Blue Shift**:\n\t- **Flashing:** Through a quick and intense increase in frequency, she can cause flashes of light akin to a firework or flashbang.\n\t- **Ionization:** The can increase the frequency of light in an area to ionize it. Concentrating it enough could leave behind radiation.\n\t- **Laser Cutting:** She can increase both the density and frequency of the light in a small area to create an intense beam, acting almost like a laser cutter.\n- **Dual Shift:**\n\t- **Disorientation:** By quickly alternating between blue and red shifting an area, she can create a disorienting field of color.\n\t- **Time Perception:** By manipulating the blue and red shift around a person to such a heavy degree, it can cause their perception of time to increase and decrease due to the doppler effect. This can cause things to look like they are moving faster or slower than they really are.\n\t- **Shockwave**: By using redshift to generate heat and slow down the atoms, but then suddenly blue shifting, the sudden increase in heat transfers into outward momentum to cool itself down, thus creating a shockwave in the area.\n- **Photon/Gravity Pressure:** Through the increasing of the density of light to an absurd degree, she can enact a gravitational pressure on the things around her. There are multiple ways to do this:\n\t- **Supercompression**: By compressing the light in an area beyond it’s limit, the pressure will cause the atoms in the area to enact fusion, creating a miniature sun which then explodes into a mini supernova.\n\t- **Gravity Hole:** By stopping the supernova and compressing even further, the energy of her supercompression folds in on itself, creating a miniature black hole. It cannot exist for long, only a second or two, but it can enact huge amounts of damage.\n\t- **Pressure Blasts:** By very rapidly increasing the density of light in an area and with a certain vector-like force, the photons in the area undergo a momentum exchange where they are thrust into the surface next to them, transferring the momentum and energy into that object. Basically pushing it out of the way. Depending on how long she spends compressing before the release, she can enact a force enough to throw someone across a room with 1G’s of force.","x":80,"y":-378,"width":767,"height":1338,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"7bc32ec9a9a562c1","type":"text","text":"## Spells\nAlex will make use of multiple spells throughout the series, but she has a main set of favorites that she likes to have on her Crest at most times.\n### Slip\n**Type:** Enchantment\n**Parameter:** Coefficient\nThis enchantment spell reduces the kinetic friction coefficient of whatever it’s used on. Most people simply use it to make things more slippery, but there are plenty of other applications.\n##### How Alex Uses It\n- She uses it on her shoes to be able to “ice-skate” around, moving faster and easier than on her feet.\n- She can push herself quickly by using shifting and creating a pocket of pressure.\n- She can compress light into hardlight to “walk on air”\n\n### Grip\n**Type:** Enchantment\n**Parameter:** Coefficient\nThe opposite to Slip, it increases the friction coefficient of whatever it touches, making it more sticky.\n\n### Echo\n**Type:** Illusion\n**Parameter:** Delay (Positive or Negative)\nThis spell creates an illusionary image of a person at the time of casting that follows the user’s movements with a delay set by the user, creating an afterimage. With enough manipulation, it can be sent “foreword” to create a theoretical projected movement.","x":880,"y":-378,"width":620,"height":378},
		{"id":"6d08a670c55f3ef3","type":"file","file":"99 - Meta/attatchments/Alex In Uniform.png","x":-920,"y":-380,"width":267,"height":400}
